      "source": "#42\n// struct_ops: build a struct/dict with N dynamic string keys, then read them\n// back using keys() and sum the values. Measures struct field write/read + keys().\n// Usage: the size N is read from stdin (one integer line).\nlet n = int(input())\nvar s = {}\nvar i = 0\nwhile i < n {\n    s[\"k${i}\"] = i * i\n    i += 1\n}\nvar total = 0\nfor k in keys(s) {\n    total += s[k]\n}\nprint(\"RESULT keys=${len(s)} total=${total}\")\n",
